---
title: Backgrounds
description: Grounds that move, slowly, for the back of a shot — the grid, the golden rectangles, the spiral, dots, a glow, a beam, rings, the twelve columns, grain, a turning gradient. A ground is felt, not watched.
eyebrow: Content creation · Elements
source: src/studio/background.css
---
<p>A background is the first layer on the timeline and the last thing anyone looks at. Each one here is a <code>span</code> behind everything (<code>im-studio-ground</code>) that moves by exactly one pitch, or one turn of the light, over forty seconds — so the loop has no seam and the eye never catches it moving. Combine two (a pattern and a glow) at most. All stop under reduced motion.</p>
