<p class="im-hint">Sped up here (8s a pitch) so the motion shows; the default is 40s.</p>

<h2>Knobs</h2>
<div class="im-table-scroll"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Default</th><th></th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>--im-studio-ground-speed</code></td><td>40s</td><td>One pitch, one turn, one pass.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>--im-pattern-size</code></td><td>2em</td><td>The pitch of the grid, the dots, the rings.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>--im-pattern-color</code></td><td>8% ink</td><td>The ink. The golden ones carry a fixed ink (an SVG tile) — use <code>opacity</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>--im-pattern-at</code></td><td>50% 40%</td><td>Where the glow sits.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>The golden ground is the same tile as <a href="/foundation/patterns/"><code>im-bg-golden</code></a> on the page; add that class beside the ground’s so the tile is there, and the ground only moves it. The grid here is the page’s grid; a frame that is measured can draw the twelve columns themselves with <code>im-studio-guides</code>.</p>
